# The B-2A's control surfaces (src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a line is
# read): each a hinge line from its inboard or lower end to its other, in the
# model's body frame, metres from its origin - +x forward, +y starboard, +z
# down - then how far forward of the hinge the part reaches, how far aft, and
# how far either side of the hinge's plane; and first the JSBSim property
# whose value, in radians, is its deflection, with which way a positive value
# moves its trailing edge.
#
# Measured off the model's own sections (assets/models/b2.mesh), by
# slicing it where each surface ends: the ailerons between 62% and 92% of the
# wing's semispan, each hinge a quarter of the local chord forward of the
# trailing edge;
# its elevators the inboard elevons, between 30% and 55% of the semispan,
# hinged as the ailerons are.
# The sections each was measured from are above its lines.
#
# wing -17.14..-11.20 at 16.19 m, -19.79..-16.88 at 24.03 m
surface left-aileron    fcs/left-aileron-pos-rad   down  -15.651 -16.191 0.133  -19.064 -24.026 0.136  0.000 1.728 0.336
surface right-aileron   fcs/right-aileron-pos-rad  down  -15.651 16.191 0.133  -19.064 24.026 0.136  0.000 1.728 0.336
# wing -19.54..-5.30 at 7.83 m, -15.92..-9.89 at 14.36 m
surface left-elevator   fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -15.980 -7.835 0.204  -14.413 -14.363 0.133  0.000 4.113 0.634
surface right-elevator  fcs/elevator-pos-rad       down  -15.980 7.835 0.204  -14.413 14.363 0.133  0.000 4.113 0.634
